lesson: 164
title: Catching up
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: When a faster traveller chases a slower one going the same way, the gap shrinks by the difference of the speeds every hour.
explain: A bus at 40 km an hour leaves 3 hours before a car at 60 km an hour. The bus is 40 × 3 = 120 km ahead.
explain: The car gains 60 − 40 = 20 km each hour, so it catches the bus after 120 / 20 = 6 hours.
vars: a=name d=5..20 m=2..4 h=2..3
let: s = d * m
let: f = d * (m + 1)
let: g = s * h
need: s >= 20 && f <= 90
answer: m * h
exercise: A bus is {g} km ahead of a car. The bus goes {s} km an hour and the car goes {f} km an hour along the same road. In how many hours does the car catch up with the bus?
exercise: A truck leaves a town at {s} km an hour. {h} hours later a car leaves the same town on the same road at {f} km an hour. How many hours after it starts does the car catch the truck?
exercise: {a}'s family drives off at {s} km an hour. {a.His} uncle sets out {h} hours later from the same house at {f} km an hour along the same way. How many hours does the uncle drive before he catches up?
exercise: A slow train is {g} km in front of a fast train, both going the same way. The slow one goes {s} km an hour, the fast one {f} km an hour. After how many hours is the fast train level with the slow one?
exercise: A boat leaves the harbour at {s} km an hour. A motorboat follows it {h} hours later at {f} km an hour. How many hours does the motorboat need to reach the boat?
test: How long, in hours, does a car going {f} km an hour need to catch a lorry going {s} km an hour that is {g} km ahead on the same road?
test: {a}'s grandfather set off in a lorry at {s} km an hour. After {h} hours {a} left the same place in a car at {f} km an hour, following the same road. How many hours did {a} drive until {a.he} reached the lorry?
test: A police car doing {f} km an hour chases a van doing {s} km an hour. The van has a {g} km start. How many hours does the chase last?
test: Two cars drive the same way. The front one, {g} km ahead, goes {s} km an hour, and the one behind goes {f} km an hour. When will the second car draw level, in hours from now?
exercise: A car going {f} km an hour is {g} km behind a bus going {s} km an hour on the same highway in Texas. How many hours does it take the car to catch up?
exercise: How many hours does a fast train at {f} km an hour need to catch a slow train at {s} km an hour that is {g} km ahead on the same track?
exercise: A van left a farm in Kansas at {s} km an hour. {h} hours later a car left the same farm at {f} km an hour along the same road. How many hours did the car drive before it caught the van?
exercise: {a} sets off in a camper van at {s} km an hour. {a.His} mum leaves home {h.words} hours later by car on the same road at {f} km an hour. After how many hours of driving does she reach {a}?
exercise: A ferry is {g} km ahead of a speedboat on a lake in Ontario. The ferry does {s} km an hour and the speedboat {f} km an hour, both the same way. In how many hours does the speedboat draw level?
exercise: Two lorries drive in the same direction on a motorway in England. The first is {g} km ahead and goes {s} km an hour; the second goes {f} km an hour. How many hours does the second need to catch the first?
exercise: A delivery truck is {g} km ahead of a car. The truck travels at {s} km per hour and the car at {f} km per hour along the same road. When does the car catch it, in hours?
exercise: A tour bus leaves Perth at {s} km an hour, and {h} hours later a car follows it from Perth at {f} km an hour. How many hours does the car take to catch the bus?
test: A truck at {s} km an hour had been on the road for {h} hours when a motorbike at {f} km an hour left the same depot to follow it. How many hours does the motorbike ride before catching the truck?
test: In how many hours will a car doing {f} km an hour reach a camper van {g} km ahead that travels at {s} km an hour in the same direction?
test: {a}'s dad drives at {f} km an hour to catch up with a coach that left the same school {h} hours earlier at {s} km an hour on the same road. How long does it take him, in hours?
test: The gap between a slow barge and a fast launch on a river in New Zealand is {g} km. Both head the same way, the barge at {s} km an hour and the launch behind it at {f} km an hour. How many hours until the launch reaches the barge?
test: A sheriff's car doing {f} km an hour chases a truck doing {s} km an hour that is {g} km ahead. How many hours does it take to catch the truck?
test: A slower train, going {s} km an hour, left a station {h} hours before a faster train, which goes {f} km an hour from the same station on the same line. After how many hours of travel does the faster train catch up?
exercise: bus is {g} km ahead, does {s} km an hour, car behind does {f}. how long til the car catches it
exercise: truck left at {s} km/h, {h+1} hours later — no wait, {h} hours later a car goes same road at {f}. how many hours the car drives til it catches it
exercise: Sam says just add the speeds. nah that's wrong innit, they're going same way. fast train {f} km/h, slow one {s} km/h and {g} km in front. hours til level?
exercise: me family left at {s} km an hour, uncle left {h} hours after at {f}, oh and we had 2 dogs in the back. how many hrs uncle drives before he catches us
test: cops doing {f} km/h chasing a van doing {s}, van's got {g} km head start. how long's the chase in hours
test: barge does {s} an hour, launch behind does {f}, gap's {g+5} km, sorry, {g} km. hours til the launch gets it
test: {a} says it's {h} hours cos {g} ÷ {s}. nah, wrong. lorry {g} km ahead at {s} km/h, car at {f} km/h same road, how many hours really
exercise: Dad was let go from the office and now drives a lorry. His lorry is {g} km behind a coach on the same road. The coach does {s} km an hour and the lorry does {f} km an hour. In how many hours does he catch the coach?
exercise: mum's been let go so we're moving in with nan. the bloody removal van's already {g} km ahead doing {s} km an hour, we're doing {f}. how many hours till we catch the stupid van
test: {a}'s old dog has "gone to live on a farm", and the van taking him is {g} km ahead, going {s} km an hour. {a}'s mum follows at {f} km an hour. After how many hours is she level with the van?
exam: It is given that a bus is {g} km in advance of a car, the bus proceeding at {s} km per hour and the car at {f} km per hour along the same road in the same direction. Determine the number of hours required for the car to overtake the bus.
exam: Whereas a lorry departs a town at {s} km per hour and, {h} hours subsequently, a car departs the same town along the same road at {f} km per hour, ascertain the number of hours, reckoned from the departure of the car, until the car overtakes the lorry.
exam: Ascertain the time in hours required for a vehicle travelling at {f} km per hour to overtake a vehicle travelling at {s} km per hour in the same direction, given that the latter commences {g} km ahead.
exam: A motorcycle travelling at {f} km per hour pursues a coach which travels at {s} km per hour and which, at the commencement of the pursuit, is {g} km ahead upon the same road. State the number of hours that shall elapse before the motorcycle draws level with the coach.
